---
import InfoPage from '../components/InfoPage.astro';
import { CONTACT } from '../config/site';

const sections = [
  {
    heading: 'Where the facts come from',
    html: `<p>Zones, Ex markings, temperature classes and the conditions of use come from ATEX and IECEx certificates, declarations of conformity and the makers' own datasheets. Specifications come from the makers' published data. Every phone page lists its sources.</p>`,
  },
  {
    heading: 'What we could not confirm',
    html: `<p>A value we could not confirm from a primary source is shown with a numbered "Unconfirmed" marker and a note at the foot of the page saying what is uncertain. When something is unknown we say it is not verified, never that the phone lacks it, and a value nobody publishes is left out.</p>`,
  },
  {
    heading: 'Same rules for every brand',
    html: `<p>Summaries, strengths, limitations and alternatives are generated by the same rules for every phone, so no brand gets kinder wording than another. Phones are listed alphabetically wherever there is no ranking.</p>
<p>Prices are shown as on request on every phone page and ranking, so price never decides where a phone sits. The cost guide quotes public reseller list prices as a benchmark only.</p>`,
  },
  {
    heading: 'How the rankings work',
    html: `<p>There are no overall scores. Each Best for page ranks phones for one zone, industry or use case, and its "How we ranked them" section states the criteria. First place has to be decided by one of those criteria, and by something visible in the data, such as the gas group, temperature class or a feature confirmed to work through a case.</p>
<p>Head-to-head comparisons give each topic to the phone with the edge, or call it even, and state the limits of both phones where they matter.</p>`,
  },
  {
    heading: 'Corrections',
    html: `<p>If a fact looks wrong, or you have a newer certificate, <a href="${CONTACT.href}">tell us</a>. We check it against the document and update the page. Always check the certificate for your exact model before taking a phone into a hazardous area.</p>`,
  },
];
---

<InfoPage
  path="/how-we-rate/"
  title="How We Rate Intrinsically Safe Phones"
  description="Where our phone data comes from, how we flag what we could not confirm, and the rules behind every ranking and head-to-head comparison."
  h1="How we rate"
  lead="The rules we apply to every phone, whoever makes it."
  sections={sections}
/>
